{
  "note": [
    "The corpus both implementations of loop-lint are run against.",
    "",
    "`tool/loop_lint.dart` in this project and `scripts/loop-lint.mjs` in every",
    "Node scaffolder are the same seven rules written twice, in two languages.",
    "Two implementations of one contract drift; these cases are what stops them",
    "drifting silently.",
    "",
    "Each case names a tree of files written to a temp dir before the linter",
    "runs. Both implementations run against the same bytes; `violations[].rule`",
    "and `violations[].match` are the contract — `match` is a substring that must",
    "appear in the rejection message, deliberately a phrase both implementations",
    "word identically, so the prose can still improve on either side without",
    "breaking the corpus.",
    "",
    "L2 is the one rule whose vocabulary is genuinely per-dialect: this project",
    "runs `dart run` and `flutter test`, the Node scaffolders run `npm run`. The",
    "corpus therefore only uses `make <target>`, which both halves resolve the",
    "same way against the same Makefile, and each side's own test covers its own",
    "dialect. A case here that passed in one language because of a form the other",
    "cannot parse would be a corpus that hides the drift it exists to catch."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "case": "inert-on-a-fresh-scaffold",
      "expect": "pass",
      "why": "The shipped templates are not contracts. A gate that failed on the seed the harness itself installed would be red in every project on day one.",
      "files": {
        "Makefile": "check:\n\ttrue\n",
        "feature_list.json": "[{\"id\":\"feature-001\",\"status\":\"not_started\"}]\n",
        "docs/loops/loop-state.schema.json": "@schema",
        "docs/loops/goal-template.json": "{\"feature\":\"ignored\"}\n",
        "docs/loops/maker-prompt.md": "# maker\n",
        "docs/loops/checker-prompt.md": "# checker\n"
      },
      "violations": []
    },
    {
      "case": "a-contract-and-a-converged-loop",
      "expect": "pass",
      "why": "The shape every rule agrees is right: a contract with an outcome, a scope, exclusions and three checks; a loop that failed once, was fixed, and passed with a result for every check.",
      "files": {
        "Makefile": "check:\n\ttrue\n\ntest:\n\ttrue\n",
        "feature_list.json": "[{\"id\":\"feature-002\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}]\n",
        "docs/loops/loop-state.schema.json": "@schema",
        "docs/loops/feature-002.goal.json": "{\"feature\":\"feature-002\",\"outcome\":\"A merchant can archive an order without opening it.\",\"scope\":[\"the archive action on the list\"],\"exclusions\":[\"bulk archive\"],\"verification\":[{\"id\":\"suite\",\"check\":\"the reducer is covered\",\"command\":\"make test\"},{\"id\":\"eye\",\"check\":\"a person looked at the row\",\"observation\":\"note in the evidence file\"}]}\n",
        "docs/loops/feature-002.loop-state.json": "{\"feature\":\"feature-002\",\"satisfied\":true,\"cycles\":[{\"n\":1,\"maker\":\"added the action\",\"checker\":{\"verdict\":\"fail\",\"results\":[{\"id\":\"suite\",\"exit\":1}]}},{\"n\":2,\"maker\":\"fixed the reducer\",\"checker\":{\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"results\":[{\"id\":\"suite\",\"exit\":0},{\"id\":\"eye\",\"note\":\"the row keeps its checkbox\"}]}}]}\n"
      },
      "violations": []
    },
    {
      "case": "L1-no-outcome",
      "expect": "violation",
      "why": "A contract with scope and checks but no outcome describes activity, not a result.",
      "files": {
        "Makefile": "check:\n\ttrue\n",
        "feature_list.json": "[{\"id\":\"feature-002\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}]\n",
        "docs/loops/loop-state.schema.json": "@schema",
        "docs/loops/feature-002.goal.json": "{\"feature\":\"feature-002\",\"scope\":[\"a thing\"],\"exclusions\":[\"another thing\"],\"verification\":[{\"id\":\"gate\",\"check\":\"green\",\"command\":\"make check\"}]}\n"
      },
      "violations": [{ "rule": "L1", "match": "has no `outcome`" }]
    },
    {
